================================================================================
smart-console — changes.log
================================================================================

2026-07-29
----------
Phase 1 (Foundation) complete. Implemented per
outputs/2026-07-29-smart-console-plan.md, Tasks 1.1-1.9, in the order
1.1 -> 1.2 -> 1.3 -> 1.5 -> 1.6 -> 1.4 -> 1.7 -> 1.8 -> 1.9 (recorder/event
bus built before the connection manager that feeds them, and before the
Cisco plugin, per architect review).

Delivered:
- 3-crate Cargo workspace (smart-console-core / smart-console-ui /
  smart-console-cli), Rust edition 2024, stable toolchain 1.97.1.
- Config loader (toml + directories), device scanner (/dev/cu.* + USB
  VID/PID -> vendor name), connection manager (dedicated-thread <->
  tokio bridge, reconnect with backoff), event bus + line assembler,
  session recorder with redaction (passwords/secrets/SNMP community
  strings never hit disk unredacted; 0600/0700 permissions set at
  creation), VendorPlugin trait + PluginRegistry + Cisco IOS/IOS XE/NX-OS
  plugin, 4-pane ratatui TUI shell, CLI (`list-devices`, `connect`).
- 74 automated tests (58 core + 16 ui), all passing. `cargo fmt --check`,
  `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, and
  `cargo test --workspace` are all clean; the unwrap/expect/panic deny
  gate was verified to actually fire (not just declared) before Task 1.1
  was considered done.
- Real-machine verification: `list-devices` and `connect --help` run for
  real on this development machine; `connect` against a nonexistent port
  produces a clean error instead of a panic; the connection manager was
  exercised over a real Unix PTY pair (not just mocks).

Explicitly NOT verified (flagged rather than silently claimed complete):
- No physical USB-serial adapter or real network device (Cisco/Dell/
  Aruba/Comware/JunOS) was available in this environment. Device scanner,
  connection manager, and the Cisco plugin's banner/prompt parsing are
  unit-tested and PTY-tested but not confirmed against real hardware.
- No real attached terminal (TTY) was available to visually run the
  interactive `connect` + TUI flow; rendering is verified via
  `ratatui::TestBackend` snapshots instead of a manual on-screen run.
- Both gaps are called out in README.md's "Known limitations" section;
  please test against real hardware/a real terminal before production use.

Deviations from the original spec, documented and justified in
outputs/2026-07-29-smart-console-design.md:
- Log timestamps use UTC, not local time -- no date/time crate is in the
  mandated dependency list, and local-timezone conversion needs one (or
  unsafe FFI). Implemented a small dependency-free UTC calendar
  conversion instead (session/time_util.rs).
- `tokio-serial` was deliberately NOT added; the serial<->tokio bridge
  uses a dedicated OS thread + channel instead, staying within the
  mandated crate list.

Post-implementation review (advisor pass before declaring Phase 1 done)
found one real defect and two decisions worth recording explicitly:
- Ctrl+C while connected set a UI-internal flag that nothing downstream
  ever read, so it did nothing observable and the "second Ctrl+C quits
  once disconnected" fallback was unreachable. Fixed: the reader thread
  now publishes Disconnected on every exit path (not just the
  too-many-errors path), and a new disconnect_tx channel forwards the
  request from the UI to the CLI's ConnectionHandle. A regression test
  (`ctrl_c_while_connected_sends_on_disconnect_tx_not_just_the_app_flag`)
  now exercises the actual wiring, not just the App struct in isolation.
- Redaction patterns didn't cover key-based credential syntax
  (key-string, authentication key, radius-server/tacacs-server key).
  Added a deliberately broad `\bkey\b` pattern -- over-redaction is the
  stated safe default for this control.
- `create_secure_dir_all` originally trusted a pre-existing log_dir's
  permissions. First fix attempt over-corrected: it tightened every
  pre-existing ancestor directory, which broke in the test environment
  (can't chmod the system temp dir) -- caught by running the suite 3x,
  not a single green run. Corrected to tighten only the leaf log_dir,
  never its ancestors.
Full suite re-verified 3x clean after all three fixes: 58 core + 16 ui
tests, fmt/clippy clean.

Next: Phase 2 (Dell OS10/Aruba CX/Comware/JunOS plugins, real-time event
classification wired into the UI, persistent history + Ctrl-R search).
